pr_comments:
The SharedLister is an interface between scheduler and Cluster Autoscaler. CA uses its own [implementation of SharedLister](https://github.com/kubernetes/autoscaler/blob/master/cluster-autoscaler/simulator/cluster_snapshot.go#L29) as a way to run Filters on in-memory NodeInfos that represent potential nodes that may be created by autoscaler. 

Moving PV-related logic into SharedLister could in principle help solve longstanding issues around autoscaling and pods using PVs (if all access to PV/PVC would actually go through the SharedLister), but we should make sure that any changes we make here are done with co-ordination with sig-autoscaling to:
 * Make sure the design is compatible with CA;
 * Necessary changes are also implemented to CA (as-is this PR will cause CA to stop compiling, as its ClusterSnapshot no longer satisfies the new interface).

